 sources:[source('Tidio pricing','https://www.tidio.com/pricing/'),source('Tidio live chat and monthly rates','https://www.tidio.com/live-chat/'),source('Tidio package guide','https://help.tidio.com/hc/en-us/articles/6266099959708-Which-upgrades-do-I-need'),source('Tidio on Lyro capabilities','https://www.tidio.com/blog/lyro-review/')],
 proof:{'live-chat':['Live chat',1],'live-typing':['Live typing preview',1],'visitor-list':['Real-time visitors',1],'automatic-replies':['Lyro AI allowance applies',3],'knowledge':['Lyro trained on your content',3],'human-takeover':['Shared inbox and human support',3],'shared-inbox':['Shared inbox; confirm project setup',3],'translation':['Multilingual Lyro; not the same as two-way operator translation',3],'team-size':['10 seats on the displayed entry tiers',0],'widget-brand':['Customizable live chat',1],'analytics':['Plan-dependent reporting',0]},
 sections:[
 s('Compare the package you will actually use.',`The word Tidio can describe several connected products. Customer Service covers the human support side, Lyro is the AI agent, and Flows provides rule-based automation. Those pieces can work together, but their allowances are not interchangeable. A comparison that takes the cheapest live-chat subscription and treats it as unlimited AI is not helping you budget.

Orka takes a different route through the purchasing decision: select the team size you need, keep unlimited projects under that subscription, and choose managed AI usage or your own provider key. The feature question is still important. Pod and Fleet include capabilities such as message search, image sharing and analytics that should not be silently assigned to Solo. Write down your actual requirements before comparing either free plan with a paid package.`,[2]),
 s('A sensible starting price is not the final bill.',`Tidio’s monthly live-chat page lists Starter at $29 and Growth from $59. Its main pricing page also displays lower monthly equivalents for annual billing. Starter includes 100 handled conversations; Growth scales to higher conversation allowances. The entry plans show ten seats. Orka Pod is also $29, but includes three people; Fleet is $99 with room for twenty. That means the same headline price can represent a very different team and usage arrangement.

If ten people occasionally help with a modest queue, Tidio’s seat allowance is a real advantage worth acknowledging. If several projects grow their support traffic, the conversation allowance deserves more attention. Move the slider, select the appropriate tier and then add the expected automation package. Do not multiply Tidio’s base price by every teammate when the published plan already includes them.`,[0,1]),
 s('Lyro, Flows and Orky solve related jobs.',`Lyro is Tidio’s AI agent trained on your content, with multilingual support and a shared-inbox connection. Flows is its separate automation product. Orky offers automatic answers, editable drafts, summaries and shortcuts, while leaving you the choice of a provider key or managed token billing. A visual rule and a generated response can both be useful; they are simply different ways to decide what happens next.

The initial free Lyro conversations are a trial allowance rather than a promise of a new free bundle every month. Renewing capacity requires the relevant purchase. For Orka, estimate input and output tokens using your actual context and answers. In both cases, try a question with missing information. A useful assistant should make the next step clear rather than confidently completing an answer it does not have. The practical test is the conversation, not just the word AI.`,[2,3]),
 s('Give the help center its own line.',`A public article library is a different feature from a private set of training answers. Orka provides both the public help center and published knowledge for Orky. Your visitors can search articles in the widget, open a branded help site and read translated content. Your team writes in Markdown, reviews automatic translations and sees when updates make another language stale. This is included in every Orka plan.

The Tidio sources reviewed here clearly document knowledge supplied to Lyro. They do not establish an equivalent hosted public help center with custom-domain publishing, collections and the same translation-maintenance workflow. We label that point unverified rather than claiming it is impossible. If self-service publishing is central to your buying decision, ask Tidio to show the customer-facing article site and editor included in your proposed package. Do not confuse Tidio’s own support website with a help center it hosts for your business.`,[3]),
 s('The live-chat basics are not an Orka monopoly.',`Tidio advertises live typing preview and a real-time visitor view. It would be misleading to put a bright Orka checkmark beside those rows and a Tidio cross simply because our own illustrations show them prominently. Both can help a human prepare for the next question. The interface, available context and plan limits determine which version feels useful in your day.

Our suggestion is to test the moment before and after a message. Can your teammate understand what the person is trying to do? Is it obvious which website they are using? Can you leave context for someone else? In Orka, project filtering, visitor attributes, private notes and assignment turn the incoming message into a shared task. Try the same sequence in Tidio. A shorter path through your frequent tasks is more meaningful than the longest list of icons.`,[1]),
 s('A shop and a portfolio of apps need different trials.',`For a shop, use a question about an item, a delivery date and a return exception. Check how much information arrives with the conversation and which actions require another tool. Do not assume that showing an order means the AI can safely alter it. For a portfolio of apps, use three websites with different documentation and ask the same ambiguous question on each. The answer should belong to the right business.

This is where Orka’s project model is particularly worth exploring. You can bring the projects into a shared inbox and keep a clear human owner. At the same time, Tidio’s automation products may fit an existing workflow you do not want to replace. Treat your trial as a rehearsal of the operating day, with a real handover and a real exception, rather than a contest to produce the most polished greeting.`),
 s('Which one would we put on your shortlist?',`Start with Orka if you want a cohesive home for several projects, approachable team pricing and public knowledge that also supports AI. Its working-hours, break-day and panic banners are useful when a small team needs honest expectations. An automated response can cover the routine question while a person handles the exception, without pretending everyone is available around the clock.

Keep Tidio on the shortlist if Lyro and Flows suit the way you already automate support, or if its entry-level seat allowance fits your team particularly well. Ask for the full package price at your expected volume, including recurring AI capacity. The winner for a ten-person team with a quiet inbox may be different from the winner for a solo founder with several busy products. That is a reason to calculate carefully, not a reason to force a universal winner.`)
 ]
