 sources:[source('Commslayer pricing and allowances','https://www.commslayer.com/pricing'),source('Commslayer product FAQ','https://docs.commslayer.com/articles/1771000257-frequently-asked-questions'),source('Commslayer customer portal','https://www.commslayer.com/customer-portal-for-shopify'),source('Commslayer helpdesk','https://www.commslayer.com/helpdesk')],
 proof:{'live-chat':['Live chat and connected channels',0],'email-follow-up':['Email support',0],'team-size':['Unlimited agents',0],'shared-inbox':['Unified commerce helpdesk',3],'assignment':['Assignment rules',0],'saved-replies':['Macros',0],'automatic-replies':['AI quotas included; limits apply',0],'ai-drafts':['Draft quotas included',0],'summaries':['Plan-dependent AI summaries',0],'translation':['Plan-dependent translation',0],'help-center':['Help center on all plans',0],'help-domain':['Custom domain on all plans',0],'multilingual-help':['Storefront language support',2],'help-auto-translation':['Automatic translation',2],'help-translation-review':['Translations editable by hand; outdated markers not verified',2],'help-collections':['Searchable articles and categories',2],'help-ai':['Articles used by AI agent',2],'sdk':['Webhooks and custom actions',0],'visitor-profile':['Shopify customer context',3],'knowledge':['Knowledge used by AI',1]},
 sections:[
 s('This is a competitor worth taking seriously.',`Commslayer’s published offering includes unlimited agents, connected support channels, AI allowances and a help center with a custom domain. It also emphasizes Shopify operations. That combination means it can be a compelling option for an ecommerce team. We are not going to hide its free plan or pretend that public documentation is available only in Orka.

Orka’s case is different: one approachable support workspace for several kinds of project, with human collaboration, visitor context, editable knowledge and a choice between managed AI and your own provider key. If your business is entirely organized around Shopify, Commslayer’s focus may be useful. If the same people support apps, bookings, services and a store, the way Orka handles projects may deserve more weight. The starting point is the shape of your work, not a manufactured feature gap.`,[0,3]),
 s('Unlimited agents do not mean unlimited usage.',`Commslayer’s free plan lists three hundred billable conversations, three hundred AI messages and three hundred drafts. Plus starts at $39 with eight hundred conversations and higher AI allowances. Scale starts at $299 with six thousand conversations. Its published overages include additional conversation and AI-message charges. Agents are unlimited, but the operational units still have limits.

Orka charges by team tier: Solo free for one person, Pod $29 for three and Fleet $99 for twenty. Managed AI is separate. For a large group that handles a modest number of questions, Commslayer’s free or entry offer can look particularly attractive. For another workload, the usage allowance may matter more than seat count. Our calculator displays the starting subscription and labels the exclusions so that a low base number is not mistaken for a guaranteed total.`,[0]),
 s('Help centers are strong common ground.',`Commslayer lists a help center and custom domain on all plans. That is a genuine overlap with Orka, and an important one: customers should be able to find routine answers without waiting for a reply. If your shortlist includes these two products, the presence of a free help center is not enough to choose between them.

Orka’s confirmed publishing workflow includes Markdown, collections and sections, article search and filters, views and reactions, SEO fields, automatic translation and manual translation edits. Source changes mark translations as outdated. Published articles appear on the help site, can be read in the widget and support Orky. Compare these maintenance details directly with the Commslayer workflow you would use. Publishing the first ten articles is the easy test; revising them in several languages after a product change is the more revealing one.`,[0,1]),
 s('Commerce actions are a meaningful differentiator.',`Commslayer’s offering documents Shopify-oriented work, including order actions and connections to subscription tools. Its customer portal currently provides articles and contact options; native portal returns, tracking and order management are labeled coming soon. Existing order-editing tools and future portal actions should not be conflated. That is a reason to evaluate the product on actual store workflows.

Orka’s current catalogue confirms cart context and visitor information, not equivalent automatic refunds, subscription management or a full self-service order portal. We do not turn those unconfirmed capabilities into a checkmark. If they are essential, ask for a demonstration before selecting Orka. If your team mainly needs accurate answers and a human decision for exceptions, the conversation and knowledge workflow may matter more than a transactional portal. Both are reasonable priorities.`,[0,2]),
 s('AI quotas and token prices tell different stories.',`Commslayer publishes included AI-message and draft quantities. Orka’s managed AI is measured using the named model’s input and output tokens, or billed directly by your provider when you bring your own key. An AI-message allowance is not a fixed amount of model context, and a draft that a person edits is not necessarily equivalent to an autonomous resolution.

Take a representative batch of work and separate three jobs: suggesting a reply, answering a routine question automatically and handing an exception to a person. Record quality and usage for each. A bundle can be convenient when the included quantities align with the workload. Token pricing can be transparent when you have measured the actual consumption. The comparison should not pretend either method predicts cost perfectly without knowing the conversations you intend to run.`,[0]),
 s('Read roadmaps as roadmaps.',`Software pages sometimes show upcoming capabilities next to available ones. Commslayer’s pricing page labels some items as coming soon. Those labels matter. A planned channel or future automation should not become a current checkmark simply because it appears in the feature list. Confirm availability in the actual account and plan you are evaluating.

Apply the same discipline to Orka. The catalogue used here contains the capabilities established in the current product brief and site, including the help-center workflow confirmed by the product owner. It is not a promise of every possible integration. During your trial, write down the exact task you expect to perform and verify it. A clear boundary is more helpful than a confident sales sentence that merges a shipped feature, a custom integration and a future idea.`,[0]),
 s('Our recommendation follows your business, not our mascot.',`Choose Commslayer when Shopify support and store actions dominate your day, especially if unlimited agents and the included usage fit your team. Its free help center and AI allowances are real reasons to consider it. Calculate the likely overages and verify the actions you need, then judge the workflow with the people who will use it.

Choose Orka when a shared crew supports several projects and wants live conversations, public knowledge and AI assistance to feel consistent across them. The working-hours and emergency banners help keep human expectations clear, while reviewed drafts let your team decide what is actually sent. An orca is a pleasant bonus, but the serious decision is whether the workspace reduces repeated context and helps you answer accurately. If a competing product does that better for your store, this comparison should make that visible.`)
 ]
